@include ../../shared/squash.overtone

## Backhand ladder volleys
@track Volleys
Backhand ladder volleys, five minutes. Start within two metres of the front wall, on your backhand
side, a metre or so off the side wall: soft volleys above the service line, hitting each one again
before it bounces. Then move back behind the tape for your volley ladder level: halfway to the short
line, three-quarters of the way, or the short line itself. Let it bounce if you lose it. The last
thirty seconds are your ladder check. Phase two target: twenty without a break from the
three-quarter line.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 5:00
0:00 [go]
7% Racket high. Punch, then extend up.
20% Firm wrist.
33% Move back to your ladder line. Serve it up, and keep volleying.
45% Racket high. Punch.
60% Lose it? Let it bounce, and serve it up again.
75% Shoulders to the side wall.
-0:30 Ladder check. Thirty seconds from your ladder line: count your best run without a break.
-0:10 Ten seconds.
---
[stop]
